  we've got Winston's details what our  conditions in the freezer like I guess  you need a lot of protein for all those  acrobatics which must be the reason that  the only thing in Lara's kitchen are  hanging carcasses of meat now given that  according to the Food and Agriculture  Organization of the United Nations meat  carcasses should be frozen at a minimum  of not degrees Fahrenheit or minus 18  degrees Celsius to last at least six  months we can deduce that Winston is in  virtue night he'd face a number of  dangers the start frostbite according to  the British National Health Service  frostbite is damage to skin and tissue  caused by exposure to freezing  temperatures typically any temperature  below minus 0.55 degrees Celsius or 31  degrees Fahrenheit the body responds to  the chill by narrowing blood vessels  blood flow to the extremities slows down  to the blood can reach vital organs  dead without the lovely warm blood  coursing through them extremities like  fingers and toes get colder and fluid  within the tissue can freeze the elderly  are particularly more susceptible to  frostbite because they have less  subcutaneous tissue that's the stuff  under the skin that's used for fat  storage which the body needs to keep  warm a way to prevent frostbite is to  wrap up warm and actually wear that hat  scarf glove and sock sets the amother  knitted you for Christmas she worked  hard on there however it's not that easy  for Winston we can see that he's wearing  his butlering attire and sadly the  uniform doesn't come with thick knitted  items to protect his head and fingers so  it seems that frostbite is a given but  what other dangers lurk inside the  freezer hypothermia occurs when your  body temperature drops below 35 degrees  C or 95 degrees Fahrenheit  normal body temperature is 37 degrees C  or 98.6 degrees Fahrenheit so while this  is only a couple of degrees it could  mean the difference between life and  death there's three stages of  hypothermia mild moderate and severe  depending on how much your body  temperature drops you'll start shivering  and hyperventilating gradually you'll  become confused speech will slur and  you'll lose coordination from there your  pulse weakens and you'll likely fall  unconscious hypothermia doesn't just  happen to people who get locked in  freezers babies and the elderly are also  at risk there have been a few cases  where people have gone out drinking late  at night without wearing appropriate  clothing and developed hypothermia I'm  from Newcastle in the north of England  and I can believe that so make sure you  keep that core temperature up if you're  locked in a freezer try and fashioned  some kind of protection from the cold  create a barrier between yourself and  the floor using cardboard boxes wrap  yourself in layers if you can sadly for  Winston this isn't really an option  Mira's freezer is so sparse he's pretty  much doomed to a bout of hypothermia  that's if he doesn't suffocate first  this is not a cheery one is it the  freezer bunker doesn't have any windows  or visible ventilation shaft  meaning that poor ol Winston could  actually suffocate there have been a few  cases where people have become trapped  in freezes and have been overcome by  carbon dioxide fumes from blocks of dry  ice which are sometimes used in giant  walk-in freezers to preserve food if the  main freezer mechanism is broken  basically when we locked Winston in the  freezer we doomed him to frostbite  hypothermia and potentially suffocation  and that's not to mention the lack of  food water and the fact that he would  have to go to the bathroom in there too  so yeah now I've made myself feel bad  well this video certainly went some  places if you ever do find yourself  going into a walk-in freezer make sure  that the emergency release works and  tell someone that you're going in there  anyway thanks for watching this week's  episode of reality check you can find me  on Twitter at Lucy James games and